# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# OAuth secrets + extracted data for experiments/ — never commit.
#
# These were the filenames a generic Google tutorial produces. This project's OWN documented
# default is ~/.csa_google_workspace/client_secret.json (mcp/_config.py, mcp/_login.py), and
# Google's console emits client_secret_<id>.apps.googleusercontent.com.json - neither of which
# any pattern here matched. History is clean (trufflehog 0/0 across 252 commits, gitleaks
# clean) and two backstops exist, the release-job sdist grep and gitleaks' own ruleset. The gap
# was that the cheapest and earliest control was the one with the hole. (#193)
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
token.json
token_full.json
token.readonly.json
# extractor / probe output may contain real comment content/emails — keep it local
experiments/anchor-probe/*.json
experiments/**/*_transcript.json

# Ruff stuff:
.ruff_cache/

# PyPI configuration file
.pypirc

# Playwright MCP scratch output (screenshots, snapshots, console logs)
.playwright-mcp/

# `.claude/` is excluded by many people's GLOBAL gitignore (it usually holds personal session
# state). Two files here are project policy and must travel with the repo, so they are
# re-included explicitly. The directory has to be un-ignored FIRST: git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/README.md

# uv regenerates this on any `uv run`, and `git add -A` then sweeps it in. A lock pins ONE
# resolution, which is the wrong artifact for a library published to PyPI and tested across a
# Python matrix - consumers resolve against their own constraints. Same call as the sibling
# csa-google-gmail-calendar.
uv.lock
